<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-I4-AI3>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-I4-AI3" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-20T23:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "Doubled 'Recovery:' line in composed AtmError messages -- 4 call sites re-embed an already-rendered error.message() (which already contains a 'Recovery:' line) into a new AtmError constructor, which appends its own second 'Recovery:' line" ;
  triage:description "FOLLOWUP CORRECTION (supersedes initial_pass root-cause analysis). The originally recorded mechanism (error_catalog.rs:10 render() vs send/mod.rs:184 caller-supplied-hint path) was INCORRECT and c553b822 ('fix(send): avoid duplicate catalog recovery guidance', guarding send/mod.rs:184 with `if !message.contains(\"Recovery:\")`) does NOT fix this finding -- that commit's only new test covers an unrelated path (WarningEntry::render in send/mod.rs), not any of the 4 real buggy sites below. AI4-QA-1 verdict (quality-mgr, corroborated by req-qa + ruthless-boundary-qa + rust-best-practices-agent + arch-qa's own re-check) re-verified the real mechanism directly: each site takes a lower-level error whose `.message()` already contains a composed 'Recovery: ...' line (rendered by error_catalog::render()) and passes that whole message string into a NEW `AtmError::new(...)` / `AtmError::caller_context_request_invalid(...)` / helper constructor call, which independently appends its own guidance-derived 'Recovery: ...' line on top -- producing 'Recovery: ... Recovery: ...' in the final composed message. This is a distinct bug from send/mod.rs:184's caller-supplied-hint path and is NOT touched by c553b822. Directly re-verified all 4 sites on feature/pAI-s4-error-consumer-migration @ baf86e22 (team-lead direct grep, 2026-07-20) and confirmed the same unfixed code is present on feature/pAI-s5-chat-address-identity @ 17bfb4c0 (AI.5 branched from AI.4 and inherits it unchanged)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "whole_phase" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/1>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/2>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/3>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/4>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/5>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-I4-AI3/pAI-4/6> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-4/baf86e22>, <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-5/17bfb4c0> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/pAI-5/17bfb4c0> ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s5-chat-address-identity" ;
  triage:highestFixedBranch "feature/pAI-s5-chat-address-identity" ;
  triage:resolution "FIXED: all 3 real sites (crates/atm-core/src/identity/hook.rs:~58, crates/atm-core/src/config/mod.rs:~99, crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs:~192) switched to error.detail() instead of error.message(); AtmError::detail() strips any prior 'Recovery:' suffix before the outer constructor renders its own, so each site now emits exactly one Recovery: line. Fixed on feature/pAI-s5-chat-address-identity @ ad8a6021, merge-forwarded through AI10 @ 8775de8d. quality-mgr independently re-verified against source (AI-fixround-2-QA-recheck, message 01KY1F2ZSX9CNYGMMNXFKVKNWX): PASS." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-20T23:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

